Reason: player->set_aim for mods (port_ext_player_aim): an extension may aim Mario's body and FLUDD a way of its own, whichever way he moves. After each tick's control, before FLUDD moves and his pose is made, his body turns that way (mModelFaceAngle); and FLUDD tilts up or down by it (TNozzleBase::calcGunAngle), as it does for the game's own L camera. A first-person camera keeps FLUDD spraying where it looks, walking sideways too. Without such an extension, nothing changes.

